{"type":"standard","title":"Algerian Arabic","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Algerian Arabic</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q56499","titles":{"canonical":"Algerian_Arabic","normalized":"Algerian Arabic","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Algerian Arabic</span></span>"},"pageid":2379261,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/WIKITONGUES-_Reda_speaking_Algerian_Arabic.webm/330px--WIKITONGUES-_Reda_speaking_Algerian_Arabic.webm.jpg","width":330,"height":186},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/WIKITONGUES-_Reda_speaking_Algerian_Arabic.webm/1920px--WIKITONGUES-_Reda_speaking_Algerian_Arabic.webm.jpg","width":1920,"height":1080},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1355169793","tid":"d1c3797a-5424-11f1-b613-e99cd4cfa362","timestamp":"2026-05-20T08:20:54Z","description":"Maghrebi dialect of the Arabic language spoken in Algeria","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algerian_Arabic","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algerian_Arabic?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algerian_Arabic?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Algerian_Arabic"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algerian_Arabic","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Algerian_Arabic","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algerian_Arabic?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Algerian_Arabic"}},"extract":"Algerian Arabic, natively known as Dziria, Darja or Derja, is a variety of Arabic spoken in Algeria. It belongs to the Maghrebi Arabic dialect continuum and is mostly intelligible with the Tunisian and Moroccan dialects. Darja (الدارجة) means 'everyday/colloquial dialect'.","extract_html":"<p><b>Algerian Arabic</b>, natively known as <b><span><i lang=\"arq-Latn\">Dziria</i></span></b>, <b><span><i lang=\"arq-Latn\">Darja</i></span></b> or <b><span><i lang=\"arq-Latn\">Derja</i></span></b>, is a variety of Arabic spoken in Algeria. It belongs to the Maghrebi Arabic dialect continuum and is mostly intelligible with the Tunisian and Moroccan dialects. <i>Darja</i> (الدارجة) means 'everyday/colloquial dialect'.</p>"}